{"title":"Walking Men Worldwide","link":"https://kottke.org/26/09/walking-men-worldwide","date":1789755000000,"content":"\n         \t<p>Artist Maya Barkai assembled a collection of pedestrian traffic signals from around the world: <a href=\"https://walking-men.com\">Walking Men Worldwide</a>.</p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690151-1ddc1a7a.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690151-1ddc1a7a.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690151-1ddc1a7a.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690183-7e6a468f.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690183-7e6a468f.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690183-7e6a468f.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690191-86bb806a.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690191-86bb806a.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690191-86bb806a.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690198-73a7288e.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690198-73a7288e.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1789690198-73a7288e.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p>I love all of these little people. The Warsaw one reminds me somewhat of Rocky from Project Hail Mary. Some of the ones from smaller places have more personality, but I feel like the New York and Boston ones are my favorites aesthetically. Weirdly, the iconic German <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ampelm%C3%A4nnchen\">Ampelmännchen</a> isn’t among the crowd here.</p>\n\t<p>A screenprint of the collected pedestrian people <a href=\"https://walking-men.com/product/hoodie-with-logo\">is available on the Walking Men Worldwide website</a>. (via <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/jessicabrillhart\">@jessicabrillhart</a>)\n</p>\n \n\n        \n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/art\">art</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/cities\">cities</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/design\">design</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Maya%20Barkai\">Maya Barkai</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/walking\">walking</a></p>\n        \n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"d90035c0bc20dd41872f450f8c02a0f83a0192be47908304b68c3ed2980a00de","category":"Sites"}